<!--
  SYNTHETIC SAMPLE — NO REAL TAXPAYER DATA. Written from scratch; all
  identities are deliberately fake.

  BRANCH PROVED: two conditions at once, both invisible in a TRY sale.

    · FOREIGN CURRENCY — DocumentCurrencyCode is USD, so the model prints the
      currency next to every amount AND prints the exchange-rate row it reads
      from cac:PricingExchangeRate/cbc:CalculationRate. A TRY document leaves
      both switched off, so nothing else in the library exercises the amount
      formatter's non-TRY path.
    · VAT EXEMPTION — the 0015 subtotal is 0 and carries a written
      cbc:TaxExemptionReason, which is what the "İstisna" explanation row prints.
      The de-duplication guard (a reason equal to a preceding one is printed
      once) is exercised too: the same reason appears at document AND line level.
-->
